  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "In this figure \\(\\angle RFS=\\angle FDR,\\) \\(FD=4\\) inches, \\(DR=6\\) inches, \\(FR=5\\) inches, and \\(FS=7\\dfrac12\\) inches. The length of \\(RS,\\) in inches, is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "undetermined"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(4\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(5\\dfrac12\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(6\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(6\\dfrac14\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "e",
    "value": "25/4"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1964-p29.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "At the equal included angles, \\[ \\begin{gathered} \\frac{FR}{FD}=\\frac54,\\\\ \\frac{FS}{DR}=\\frac{15}{12}=\\frac54. \\end{gathered} \\] Thus \\(\\triangle RFS\\sim\\triangle FDR\\) by SAS. Side \\(RS\\) corresponds to \\(FR=5,\\) so \\(RS=(\\frac{5}{4})\\cdot5=\\frac{25}{4}=6\\frac14.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Compare triangles \\(RFS\\) and \\(FDR\\) around the marked equal angles",
        "The adjacent side ratios are \\(\\frac{5}{4}=\\frac{15}{12}\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
